  <h1>Care Instructions</h1>
  <p class="page-intro">Treat the garment right and the print will outlast the trend. A few simple habits keep your 4DA gear looking sharp for years.</p>

  <h2>Washing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Turn it inside out</strong> before washing to protect the print.</li>
    <li>Machine wash <strong>cold</strong> (max 30&deg;C / 86&deg;F) on a gentle cycle.</li>
    <li>Wash with <strong>like colors</strong>. Black pieces are best washed with other darks.</li>
    <li>Use a mild detergent. <strong>Skip the bleach</strong> and skip fabric softener &mdash; softener builds up and dulls the print.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Drying</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hang dry or tumble dry low.</strong> High heat is the fastest way to shrink cotton and stress a print.</li>
    <li>Reshape hoodies and crewnecks while damp so the ribbing keeps its form.</li>
    <li>Don't dry-clean.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ironing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Iron inside out on a <strong>low</strong> setting if needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Never iron directly over the print.</strong> If you must press the front, place a cloth between the iron and the design.</li>
    <li>Avoid steam directly on the graphic.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it matters</h2>
  <p>Our designs use a durable direct-to-garment / DTFlex process that bonds into the fabric rather than sitting on top of it. It's built to resist cracking and peeling &mdash; but heat and harsh chemicals are its only real enemies. Cold wash, low heat, inside out. That's the whole secret.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>The one-line version:</strong> Inside out &middot; cold wash &middot; hang or tumble low &middot; no bleach, no softener, no ironing the print.
  </div>

